      propertyPath: NarrationEN
      value: Wrapped snugly around the air sac is a capillary, the tiniest blood
        vessel. Blood flows through it right next to the air. This is where the magic
        swap happens - the blood grabs oxygen and drops off carbon dioxide. They're
        so close, the gases only have a whisker to travel!
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
