    - target: {fileID: 1041273874672768176, guid: 78157a230b467b94da050f2e65187544, type: 3}
      propertyPath: NarrationEN
      value: 'This is the alveolar wall - the thin barrier between the air in your
        lungs and your blood. It''s so thin and delicate that gases can zip straight
        across it: oxygen goes into the blood, and carbon dioxide comes out to be
        breathed away. It''s the perfect trading window!'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 1041273874672768176, guid: 78157a230b467b94da050f2e65187544, type: 3}
      propertyPath: DescriptionEN
      value: The thin wall where oxygen and carbon dioxide swap places.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
